msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.8.md:105
msgid ""
"(This is used to implement `nix-install-package`, which is therefore immune "
"to evolution in the Nix expression language.)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.8.md:108
msgid "Install an already built store path directly:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.8.md:112
msgid ""
"Install the result of a Nix expression specified as a command-line argument:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.8.md:117
msgid ""
"The difference with the normal installation mode is that `-E` does not use "
"the `name` attributes of derivations. Therefore, this can be used to "
"disambiguate multiple derivations with the same name."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.8.md:122
msgid ""
"A hash of the contents of a store path is now stored in the database after a "
"successful build. This allows you to check whether store paths have been "
"tampered with: `nix-store         --verify --check-contents`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.8.md:127
msgid ""
"Implemented a concurrent garbage collector. It is now always safe to run the "
"garbage collector, even if other Nix operations are happening simultaneously."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.8.md:131
msgid ""
"However, there can still be GC races if you use `nix-instantiate` and `nix-"
"store                 --realise` directly to build things. To prevent races, "
"use the `--add-root` flag of those commands."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.8.md:136
msgid ""
"The garbage collector now finally deletes paths in the right order (i.e., "
"topologically sorted under the “references” relation), thus making it safe "
"to interrupt the collector without risking a store that violates the closure "
"invariant."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.8.md:141
msgid ""
"Likewise, the substitute mechanism now downloads files in the right order, "
"thus preserving the closure invariant at all times."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.8.md:144
msgid ""
"The result of `nix-build` is now registered as a root of the garbage "
"collector. If the `./result` link is deleted, the GC root disappears "
"automatically."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.8.md:148
msgid ""
"The behaviour of the garbage collector can be changed globally by setting "
"options in `/nix/etc/nix/nix.conf`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.8.md:151
msgid ""
"`gc-keep-derivations` specifies whether deriver links should be followed "
"when searching for live paths."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.8.md:154
msgid ""
"`gc-keep-outputs` specifies whether outputs of derivations should be "
"followed when searching for live paths."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.8.md:157
msgid ""
"`env-keep-derivations` specifies whether user environments should store the "
"paths of derivations when they are added (thus keeping the derivations "
"alive)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.8.md:161
msgid "New `nix-env` query flags `--drv-path` and `--out-path`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.8.md:163
msgid ""
"`fetchurl` allows SHA-1 and SHA-256 in addition to MD5. Just specify the "
"attribute `sha1` or `sha256` instead of `md5`."
msgstr ""

